        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/n/e274bd/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-03-04T16:55:01.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hi!  We played our first games of Sentinels last night and wanted to make sure we interpreted something correctly.</p>\n<p>On the “Play a Card” phase I can take a one-shot attack card and put it into play, but not use that power on the “Use a Power” phase, thus saving it for a later round (when I might be blocked from playing a card or want to get an Ongoing into play and still attack).</p>\n<p>Were we correct?</p>\n<p>Thank you!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:11.598Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 5514,
        "topic_slug": "verifying-playing-a-card-vs-using-a-power-for-one-shot-powers",
        "display_username": "Nicosomething",
        "primary_group_name": null,
        "flair_name": null,
        "flair_url": null,
        "flair_bg_color": null,
        "flair_color": null,
        "flair_group_id": null,
        "badges_granted": [],
        "version": 1,
        "can_edit": false,
