      {
        "id": 26249,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-03-05T03:55:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;SlenderTroll&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"SlenderTroll\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>As far as I know, there is no such thing as a One-Shot Power.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Slender Troll’s description is accurate - technically, there’s no such thing as a One-Shot Power.</p>\n<p>Hopefully this won’t confuse the issue, but there are Powers that cause the card to be destroyed (i.e., put in the discard pile), so it’s only useable once, but it isn’t a One-Shot - the card stays in play until that Power is activated (or something else gets rid of it). 8)</p>\n<p>Rabit</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:00:11.113Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
